  chatPanels:
  - {fileID: 399620762}
  - {fileID: 1832718962}
  - {fileID: 795620915}
  - {fileID: 1561098587}
  - {fileID: 266755700}
  acceptedId: 
  explorerScript: {fileID: 340016444}
  artInspectorScript: {fileID: 1577869089}
  day1Container: {fileID: 222006168}
  day2Container: {fileID: 1394162647}
  day2ProfileButtons:
  - {fileID: 428345871}
  - {fileID: 1114383431}
  - {fileID: 541248100}
  - {fileID: 101606290}
  - {fileID: 1841180480}
  interviewDatabase:
  - candidateId: 0
    candidateName: Pen Godes
    profilePicture: {fileID: -7632330919033245557, guid: d404b240ddec7c145aedef5d59df7793, type: 3}
    defaultGreeting: SOO... WHAT WANNA YOU ASK HUH???
    answers:
    - "Mona Lisa? That\u2019s not a masterpiece. That\u2019s just a painting of woman
      without eyebrows. I don\u2019t find it entertaining.\n"
    - Of course I would refuse! What sane person would do revision under 1 hour?
      It should have been impossible if you put that in the contract!
    - "I\u2019m a God of Art. There\u2019s not art block in my dictionary."
    - Happiness?? Easy, draw smiling face! :)
    - Do the project that I want to do first
  - candidateId: 1
    candidateName: Alvicia Roxcie
    profilePicture: {fileID: -3129907467348580636, guid: 3d91b2a5c89f9454ba75be5102904827, type: 3}
    defaultGreeting: Hey hey HR, am i going to get accepted?
    answers:
    - "She\u2019s a great example of classic oil rendering, but if a client brought
      that to me today, I'd tell them the background scale is completely off and
      needs a serious crop to fix the focus."
    - "I\u2019d flat out say no. An hour before a launch is for final quality checks,
      not structural redesigns."
    - I would get out of the office. I believe that taking a short walk is a good
      way to cure art block.
    - 'Clean typography, a minimal layout, and absolutely zero clutter.

'
    - I would organize those projects first. A lot of projects can be overwhelming
      to see after all.
  - candidateId: 2
    candidateName: Alan Dezain
    profilePicture: {fileID: 1456087244435955026, guid: 7073a65567364da46b642c9aac84551c, type: 3}
    defaultGreeting: Hello Sir, my name is Alan. Im ready to get Interview
    answers:
    - 'As a designer, I see her as the ultimate masterclass in lighting. The way
      Leonardo used sfumato to make her smile look different depending on where you
      look is just breathtaking

'
    - 'Honestly? I''d panic for five seconds, then call the client immediately. I''d
      ask what part of the ''feel'' is wrong, because changing the whole layout in
      one hour is straight up suicide. We need to compromise.

'
    - I'd step away from the computer, take a short walk, and grab some coffee. Forcing
      it makes it worse. Then I'd look at non-design things like architecture or
      street photography to trigger my brain.
    - "I'd use a warm, vibrant color palette\u2014like soft yellows and pastel oranges.
      I'd design a chaotic but cozy scene, maybe a crowded coffee shop with messy
      lines to show life and warmth."
    - I'd prioritize them based on complexity. I'll spend the first few days just
      sketching and planning, then tackle the hardest project first while my brain
      is still fresh.
  - candidateId: 3
    candidateName: Dimas Budiman
    profilePicture: {fileID: 4652132516395477126, guid: ea3d4c01c7cdf234d9dd0a1054ced29b, type: 3}
    defaultGreeting: 'Whatsapp Sir HR, introduce my self that my name is Dimas Budiman.
      Im here to get Designer position, and where am i going to start? '
    answers:
    - Masterpiece. I really love that Mona Lisa, especially the color. Also, I like
      how Leonardo da Vinci paints her, especially her face. He managed to capture
      her beauty perfectly!
    - "I would tell the client that it\u2019s realistically impossible. While I can
      do small tweaks like changing the fonts, redo all of the design is impossible.
      It would take days!"
    - "I would stop drawing first, then make a coffee. Art block means I\u2019m stressed
      and I need to relax first before continuing my job."
    - 'Of course with yellow paint. Yellow is often used to describe happiness. Then,
      I would make it very cartoonish since children is often associated with happiness.

'
    - I would spend an hour or two to organize those projects first. Some projects
      might takes time more than others so I would prioritize that first.
  - candidateId: 4
    candidateName: Taylor Coleman
    profilePicture: {fileID: 4592424565160850918, guid: 209abb90797bd1e45af3b7f730061117, type: 3}
    defaultGreeting: Hi HR, i'd like to get interview right now!
    answers:
    - "Honestly, she\u2019s iconic because of the mystery, but design-wise, it's
      all about the composition and the triangular structure that keeps your eyes
      locked onto her face."
    - "I would tell them it\u2019s impossible to redo everything in 1 hour. I'd offer
      to tweak the colors or typography instead of a total redesign. Let's be realistic
      here."
    - I'd blast some music, scroll through my old discarded sketches, and try to
      recycle an old idea that fits the current brief.
    - "Dynamic curves and bold typography. I\u2019d create an abstract pattern where
      all lines point upwards, giving a subconscious sense of growth and energy."
    - "I'd break my days into blocks. Project A and B in the morning, Project C in
      the afternoon. I can't focus on one thing for too long or I\u2019ll burn out!"
  interviewPanel: {fileID: 1765448083}
  headerCandidateName: {fileID: 2054529709}
  headerProfileImage: {fileID: 1414991564}
  dialogText: {fileID: 728805250}
  questionButtons:
  - {fileID: 1732874401}
  - {fileID: 672047357}
  - {fileID: 556216847}
  - {fileID: 2135232032}
  - {fileID: 1768036362}
  finalHiredId: -1
